      "side": 1,
      "message": "In the latest version I\u0027m using of_irq_find_parent() for IPIs, and I removed the phandle from the \"ipi-range\" property.\n\nCan you elaborate on why \"interrupt-default-template\" plus \"interrupt-default-range\" would be better than \"ipi-range\"?  It doesn\u0027t seem like they would be useful for anything other than IPIs.  Also, if I understand correctly, Marc doesn\u0027t want the number of arguments that irq_create_of_mapping() takes for IPIs explicitly encoded into the device tree, but rather the device tree should just specify the IPI numbers, and the Trusty driver should know the correct way to request them.",
